  "id": "COMPOUND:26749 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid and M19-MEL, mediated through multiple targets. This compound is identified as a target of several compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and Javanicoside F, all of which are known to interact with Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. These kinases, in turn, are targets of multiple compounds, with M19-MEL being a common downstream target across these pathways. The integration of these evidence points indicates that 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid may act through a series of kinase pathways to influence M19-MEL, potentially through direct or indirect interactions. The recurring involvement of kinase targets and the shared downstream effect on M19-MEL suggest a possible mechanism involving kinase activation or modulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
